  + // SessionCapTool — session-wide call-count circuit breaker
  + // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  + 
  + /// Session-wide cap on calls to high-fan-out tools (`web_search`, `sub_agent`).
  + /// Matches Claude Code's runaway-loop circuit breaker (200 calls/session).
  + /// Far above any legitimate interactive session's usage — a normal user never
  + /// hits it; only a runaway search/delegation loop does.
  + pub(crate) const SESSION_TOOL_CALL_CAP: usize = 200;
  + 
  + /// A wrapper tool that enforces a session-wide cap on how many times the inner
  + /// tool may be called. Once the cap is exceeded, every further call returns an
  + /// error result (never a panic, never a silent no-op) explaining why the tool
  + /// stopped working — the model must see the reason.
  + ///
  + /// The counter is per-process, which is the right scope for both the REPL and
